+- [ ] **REC-007**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit edit naming the visit's current revision as its base, the system SHALL store it as a new revision, make it the visit's current revision, and mark the replaced revision superseded.
+- [ ] **REC-008**: When an authenticated worker submits a visit edit naming a base revision of that visit other than the current revision, the system SHALL store it as a competing revision, leave the current revision unchanged, and mark the visit as having unresolved review work.
+- [ ] **REC-009**: When a visit edit names as its base a revision that does not exist or belongs to a different visit, the system SHALL reject the submission without creating a revision.
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a visit edit omits a base revision while the visit already exists, the system SHALL reject the submission without creating a revision.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a visit's first submission arrives, the system SHALL create the visit and store the submission as its initial current revision.
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a visit's first submission names a plot that is not active in the catalog, the system SHALL reject the submission without creating the visit.
+- [ ] **REC-013**: When a submission of an existing visit names a plot other than the visit's creation plot, the system SHALL reject the submission without creating a revision.
+- [ ] **REC-014**: When a submission is rejected, the system SHALL retain no copy of it and SHALL name the rejection reason in the response.
+- [ ] **REC-015**: When a visit submission is accepted, the system SHALL report whether it became the current revision (including its revision ID) or a competing revision (including the visit's current revision ID).
+- [ ] **REC-016**: The system SHALL enforce idempotency-key uniqueness per submitting worker.
+- [ ] **REC-017**: When a coordinator resolves a visit's competing revisions by adopting a competing revision, the system SHALL mark that revision current, mark all other competing revisions resolved-out, and mark the previously current revision superseded.
+- [ ] **REC-018**: When a coordinator adopts the visit's current revision as the resolution outcome, the system SHALL leave it current, mark all competing revisions resolved-out, and supersede nothing.
+- [ ] **REC-019**: When a coordinator supplies a corrected payload as the resolution outcome, the system SHALL validate it as a visit submission, record it with the coordinator as author and the current revision as its base, make it the visit's current revision, mark all competing revisions resolved-out, and mark the previously current revision superseded.
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When a resolution names a visit with no unresolved review work, or names a revision that does not exist or belongs to a different visit, the system SHALL reject the resolution and change no revision states.
+- [ ] **REC-021**: When two resolutions for the same visit are processed concurrently, the system SHALL apply the first processed and reject any later resolution naming revisions that are no longer competing.
+- [ ] **REC-022**: When a resolution is attempted without an authenticated coordinator, the system SHALL reject it.
+- [ ] **REC-023**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL return each revision's ID, per-visit sequence number, author, receipt time, base revision, and status.
+- [ ] **REC-024**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL return, for each revision that became current through a resolution, the resolving coordinator's identity, the contributing revision IDs, and the resolution time.
